                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "918f7cce-d6e8-3c44-b9e1-91ccccc88c7f",
                        "entry_id": "09453fbb-2f8c-3833-a609-e6158acde303",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To treat with insulin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f69cad57-12fe-4aab-bd63-9856145fe326",
                                "sense_id": "918f7cce-d6e8-3c44-b9e1-91ccccc88c7f",
                                "text": "The decrease in insulin binding with improved metabolic control may be a result of the peripheral hyperinsulinemia required to insulinize the liver effectively when insulin is administered by a peripheral route."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d24ccd1-55f6-4790-922c-1a789ed8fae7",
                                "sense_id": "918f7cce-d6e8-3c44-b9e1-91ccccc88c7f",
                                "text": "by the principles of good preventive pediatrics make an early diagnosis of IDDM before complete beta-cell destruction has occurred; at the first evidence of sustained hyperglycemia, hospitalize the child, and initiate insulin therapy and adequately insulinize the child using the principles and dosages found in Chapters 5 and 6."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f68a7a5-3327-4770-a223-2362ee82e7c6",
                                "sense_id": "918f7cce-d6e8-3c44-b9e1-91ccccc88c7f",
                                "text": "There is strong evidence suggesting that an oral insulin product would provide insulin in a more physiological manner, with a resultant decrease in peripheral insulin concentration and that it would more adequately insulinize the liver."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae042c81-abae-4d14-b603-cad61c07e06d",
                                "sense_id": "918f7cce-d6e8-3c44-b9e1-91ccccc88c7f",
                                "text": "One also has to be extremely careful not to over-insulinize a patient with too much basal insulin, which can lead to significant glycemic variability and hypoglycemia."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
